oon</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Books from New York (state)|Scans from the Internet Archive/unverified|PD US expired|Scans from the Internet Archive|Books published in London|Books uploaded by F\u00e6|Books without Wikidata item|California Digital Library|Books from the United States PDF files","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nRaphael, Albert</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<div class=\"description\">\nSubjects: Astrology</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<dl><dd><a href=\"//archive.org/details/earthologyhumani00raph\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"iarchive:earthologyhumani00raph\"><bdi class=\"description en\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">Internet Archive identifier:</bdi> earthologyhumani00raph</a></dd>\n<dd><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://archive.org/download/earthologyhumani00raph/earthologyhumani00raph.pdf\">https://archive.org/download/earthologyhumani00raph/earthologyhumani00raph.pdf</a></dd></dl>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"92423862":{"pageid":92423862,"ns":6,"title":"File:Free-Electron Laser (FEL) utilization in space applications (ship-borne pointing accuracy, deep-space communications, and orbital debris tracking) (IA freeelectronlase1094510710).pdf","index":5,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":3611546,"width":1275,"height":1650,"pagecount":138,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Free-Electron_Laser_%28FEL%29_utilization_in_space_applications_%28ship-borne_pointing_accuracy%2C_deep-space_communications%2C_and_orbital_debris_tracking%29_%28IA_freeelectronlase1094510710%29.pdf/page1-960px-thumbnail.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":2400,"thumbheight":3106,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Free-Electron_Laser_%28FEL%29_utilization_in_space_applications_%28ship-borne_pointing_accuracy%2C_deep-space_communications%2C_and_orbital_debris_tracking%29_%28IA_freeelectronlase1094510710%29.pdf/page1-960px-thumbnail.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":2400,"height":3106},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/Free-Electron_Laser_%28FEL%29_utilization_in_space_applications_%28ship-borne_pointing_accuracy%2C_deep-space_communications%2C_and_orbital_debris_tracking%29_%28IA_freeelectronlase1094510710%29.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Free-Electron_Laser_(FEL)_utilization_in_space_applications_(ship-borne_pointing_accuracy,_deep-space_communications,_and_orbital_debris_tracking)_(IA_freeelectronlase1094510710).pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/92423862","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2020-07-20 18:20:12","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"<div class=\"fn\">\nFree-Electron Laser (FEL) utilization in space applications (ship-borne pointing accuracy, deep-space communications, and orbital debris tracking)</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD US Government|FEDLINK - United States Federal Collection|Scans from the Internet Archive/unverified|CC-PD-Mark|Scans from the Internet Archive|Books uploaded by F\u00e6|Books without Wikidata item","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nWittrock, Jason M.</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<div class=\"description\">\n<p>The U.S. Navy is currently conducting research which will support the production of a MW-class free-electron laser (FEL). The Navy's end-state goal is to design and implement a defense system capable of destroying a fast-flying, anti-ship cruise missile (ASCM) target. To this end, the necessity of ensuring accurate pointing control of the beam is required. The first part of this thesis focuses on the U.S. Navy's desired end-state and investigates the ability of feedback and feed-forward control methods to provide improved pointing accuracy to a beam director mounted on a naval vessel similar in size to that of a Ticonderoga-class cruiser while traversing through various sea-states. The second part of this thesis examines the feasibility of employing the FEL as a means of deep-space (Mars and beyond) communication and orbital debris removal and tracking of objects in low-earth orbit (LEO).\n</p>\n<br>Subjects: Space debris.; Free-Electron Laser; FEL; Pointing Accuracy; Space Communications; Orbital Debris Removal; Orbital Debris Tracking;</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<dl><dd><a href=\"//archive.org/details/freeelectronlase1094510710\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"iarchive:freeelectronlase1094510710\"><bdi class=\"description en\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">Internet Archive identifier:</bdi> freeelectronlase1094510710</a></dd>\n<dd><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://archive.org/download/freeelectronlase1094510710/freeelectronlase1094510710.pdf\">https://archive.org/download/freeelectronlase1094510710/freeelectronlase1094510710.pdf</a></dd></dl>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"This publication is a work of the U.S. Government as defined in Title 17, United States Code, Section 101. As such, it is in the public domain, and under the provisions of Title 17, United States Code, Section 105, may not be copyrighted.","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"196603269":{"pageid":196603269,"ns":6,"title":"File:Friends' review; a religious, literary and miscellaneous journal (IA friendsreviewrel01lewi).pdf","index":10,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":342637966,"width":966,"height":1533,"pagecount":854,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Friends%27_review%3B_a_religious%2C_literary_and_miscellaneous_journal_%28IA_friendsreviewrel01lewi%29.pdf/page1-960px-Friends%27_review%3B_a_religious%2C_literary_and_miscellaneous_journal_%28IA_friendsreviewrel01lewi%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":2400,"thumbheight":3809,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Friends%27_review%3B_a_religious%2C_literary_and_miscellaneous_journal_%28IA_friendsreviewrel01lewi%29.pdf/page1-960px-Friends%27_review%3B_a_religious%2C_literary_and_miscellaneous_journal_%28IA_friendsreviewrel01lewi%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":2400,"height":3809},"u